#X text 88 13 float: 1 to start advancing the sequencer \, 0 to stop it \; reset: reset the sequencers back to step 0 \; step_rate <f>: set clock mult. factor (0=4x \, 1=2x \, 2=1x \, 3=1/2x) \; steps <f>: base pattern length \; hits <f>: base pattern n hits (values from 0 to 1 where 0 means "no hits" and 1 means "hit on every step") \; shift <f>: base pattern shift (values from 0 to 1 where 0 means "no shift" and 1 means "shift pattern by X \, where X = length -1) \; jitter_level <f>: velocity values range while jittering (values from 0 to 1 where 0 means "No jitter" and 1 means "random velocities between 0 and jitter_ceil. any value in netween lowers the velocity floor value) \; jitter_ceil <f>: maximum velocity value while jittering (0.0-1.0) \; accent_hits <f>: quantity accented hits (values from 0 to 1 where 0 means "no accents" and 1 means "accent on every hit") \; accent_intensity <f>: the higher this value \, the higher the velocity on accent \; accent_shift <f>: shift the accents pattern by N \; pan_hits <f>: quantity of hits that are panned to pan_side (values from 0 to 1 where 0 means "no panning" and 1 means "all hits are panned to pan_side") \; pan_spread <f>: the spread between each stereo channel (values from 0 to 1 where 0 means "always centered" and 1 means "either 100% to the R or to the L") \; pan_side <f>: the stereo channel to lean to on every panner hit (0 = L \, 1 = R). all other hits lean to the opposite channel, f 176;
